<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18707" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄχθος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εος</span>, τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>burden, load,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				12.452
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Op.</u>
				692
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Tyrt.
				6
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄχθεα δυνατώτεραι
			φέρειν,</span> of camels, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				3.102
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				1.80
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ra.</u>
				9
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				4.115
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. οὐκ εὐάγκαλον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					352
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. ἀρούρης</span>
			<i>cumberers</i> of the ground, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				18.104
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				20.379
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περισσὸν ἄ. γυναικῶν</span>
			<i>plague</i> of women, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>El.</u>
				1241
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γῆς ἄλλως ἄχθη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Tht.</u>
					176d
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. μυρία γαίης</span>”
				<i>pests,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nic.
					<u>Th.</u>
					9
				</span></i>
			: but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φίλτατον ἄχθος,</span> of a
			corpse, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				379
			</span></i> (lyr.): metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δίδυμον
			ἄ.</span> double <i>burden</i> of praise, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>N.</u>
				6.57
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>load of grief,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χάρμα καὶ ἄ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Sc.</u>
					400
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπὸ φροντίδος ἄ. . . βαλεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					166
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λύπης ἄ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>El.</u>
					120
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ant.</u>
				1172
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φέρειν ἄχθη κακῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>IT</u>
					710
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. φέρειν</span> bring or cause
				<i>sorrow,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Ep.</u>
				1
			</span></i>.</div>
